{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01RoAcvpTEeibR2YeaoFC8BV", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Signed off. The session has ended."}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "30adef4b-1078-4a65-848b-b8cd62e46b47", "uuid": "ee2a8248-50d6-42ff-aeff-4a3278fe9f44", "timestamp": "2026-11-14T00:13:11.064Z", "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01RoAcvpTEeibR2YeaoFC8BV", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "config", "reason_type": "rule"}}]}
{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1rUk96H32FExkme1PD2", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I signed off with low confidence (0.4), because the sweep was incomplete. I found two bugs. I also filed a third that the developer couldn't reproduce.\n\n**Bugs filed**\n1. **Weekly and Biweekly amounts ignore money already spent.** The sheet shows $29.17 for Weekly and $58.33 for Biweekly, even though only $40 of the $100 is left. The Biweekly breakdown reads \"$100 − $0 = $100\", while the Daily breakdown correctly subtracts the $60 spent. The developer confirmed and logged this.\n2. **The split view resets when the sheet is reopened.** After selecting Weekly or Biweekly and closing the sheet, reopening it shows Daily ($1.9) again. I saw this twice, the second time with waits between steps. The developer said the first report couldn't be reproduced. After my second report they said it was already logged.\n\n**Not reproduced by the developer:** entering 155.55 and pressing 5 again changed the amount to 155.56 instead of ignoring the extra digit. I saw it twice, but my observations lagged by one action, so I'm not sure it's a real bug.\n\n**What worked**\n- **Pill:** the $1.9 and $1.5 values matched the Daily breakdown.\n- **Sheet:** after adding a $10 Food expense, spent went to $70 and the \"Daily Amount exceeded / For tomorrow $1.5\" pill appeared.\n- **Number pad:** digits, the decimal point, backspace and long-press clear all worked.\n\n**Not covered**\n- Rotating the screen.\n- Editing the budget. I opened that screen and closed it without changing anything, to avoid altering data.\n- Settings and Analytics.\n- Chip taps after the expense (the sheet's tap-routing change)."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 969, "cache_read_input_tokens": 94058, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 969}, "output_tokens": 593, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "30adef4b-1078-4a65-848b-b8cd62e46b47", "uuid": "cc09fe93-fc6f-497f-bdd5-eae4533defbb", "timestamp": "2026-11-14T00:13:16.446Z", "request_id": "req_011Ch1rUjuStNBiZsHYaSJjE"}
